# End-to-End Test Automation Framework: Complete Implementation Blueprint

> [!NOTE]
> This document serves as the **master architecture, folder hierarchy, and step-by-step implementation blueprint** for building enterprise-grade, reusable Playwright + Python automation frameworks for any web application (with specialized optimizations for Angular, React, and Vue applications).

---

## 📂 1. Exact Folder Hierarchy

When setting up a new automation project, recreate this exact folder and file structure:

```text
<Project_Root>/
│
├── .agents/
│   └── AGENTS.md                    # Framework automation rules, lessons learned & locator strategies
│
├── <app_name>_test/                 # Main test suite package (e.g., abc_test/)
│   │
│   ├── conftest.py                  # Pytest fixtures, viewport configuration & browser launch options
│   ├── requirements.txt             # Python dependencies (playwright, pytest, openpyxl, faker)
│   ├── generate_test_cases.py       # Scaffolding engine to generate structured Excel test cases
│   │
│   ├── data/
│   │   ├── urls.py                  # Centralized base domains, route paths, full URLs & dynamic route builders
│   │   ├── test_data.py             # Default test constants, form inputs, static values, credentials
│   │   └── dummy_bank_proof.jpg     # Mock files / assets for upload test steps
│   │
│   ├── pages/                       # Page Object Model (POM) Layer
│   │   ├── base_page.py             # Core Playwright wrapper (js_click, slow_fill, full-page screenshots)
│   │   ├── browse_fund_page.py      # Feature/Page Object 1
│   │   ├── validate_pan_page.py     # Feature/Page Object 2
│   │   ├── folio_details_page.py    # Feature/Page Object 3
│   │   ├── identify_yourself_page.py# Feature/Page Object 4
│   │   └── investor_details_page.py # Feature/Page Object 5
│   │
│   ├── utils/                       # Shared Utilities
│   │   ├── data_generator.py        # Dynamic test data generators (Faker, random mobile, PAN, email)
│   │   ├── excel_manager.py         # OpenPyXL manager for reading/writing execution statuses & formatting
│   │   └── excel_utils.py           # Additional excel helpers, formula handlers, cell stylers
│   │
│   ├── screenshots/                 # Auto-generated runtime screenshots organized by Page Object name
│   │   ├── BrowseFundPage/
│   │   ├── IdentifyYourselfPage/
│   │   └── InvestorDetailsPage/
│   │
│   └── tests/                       # Test Runners Layer
│       ├── test_invest_flow.py      # Pytest E2E live visual test suite (headed / slowmo execution)
│       └── run_excel_tests.py       # Data-driven background execution engine running test cases from Excel
│
├── command.txt                      # CLI quick-reference cheat sheet for running tests
├── uat script.txt                   # Manual test requirements / original test specification notes
└── implementation_plans/            # Architectural blueprints & implementation guides
    ├── centralized_url_management_blueprint.md
    ├── folderwise_screenshot_store.md
    ├── full_page_screenshot_logic.md
    ├── playwright_viewport_fix.md
    └── end_to_end_project_implementation_plan_blueprint.md
```

---

## 🏗️ 2. Core Architectural Components & Responsibilities

| Component | Directory / File | Core Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **URL Centralization** | `data/urls.py` | Single source of truth for base domains (DEV, UAT, PROD), portal route prefixes, and dynamic href links. |
| **Static Test Data** | `data/test_data.py` | Separates user input data (names, IDs, dropdown labels, test constants) from test logic. |
| **Dynamic Data Engine**| `utils/data_generator.py` | Generates random, unique values (mobile numbers, emails, timestamps) per test run to prevent collision. |
| **Base Page Wrapper** | `pages/base_page.py` | Encapsulates Playwright interactions, full-page screenshots, JS click bypasses for overlays, and smart waits. |
| **Page Objects (POM)** | `pages/*_page.py` | Encapsulates page elements, locators, and user action workflows per screen. |
| **Excel Generator** | `generate_test_cases.py` | Programmatically scaffolds test matrix workbooks (Positive, Negative, Boundary cases) with styling. |
| **Data-Driven Engine** | `tests/run_excel_tests.py` | Executes tests directly against Excel rows, asserting outcomes and writing back PASS/FAIL results. |
| **Pytest E2E Runner** | `tests/test_*_flow.py` | Full linear user journey tests runnable with `--headed`, `--slowmo`, or in CI/CD. |

---

## ⚡ 3. End-to-End Step-by-Step Implementation Guide

Follow these 8 steps to bootstrap an identical project from scratch:

### Step 1: Environment Initialization & Dependencies
1. Create project folder and virtual environment:
   ```bash
   mkdir my_new_project
   cd my_new_project
   python -m venv venv
   # Windows:
   .\venv\Scripts\activate
   # Linux/Mac:
   source venv/bin/activate
   ```
2. Create `<app_name>_test/requirements.txt`:
   ```text
   playwright>=1.40.0
   pytest>=7.4.0
   pytest-playwright>=0.4.0
   openpyxl>=3.1.0
   faker>=20.0.0
   requests>=2.31.0
   ```
3. Install dependencies and download browser binaries:
   ```bash
   pip install -r abc_test/requirements.txt
   playwright install chromium
   ```

---

### Step 2: Browser & Pytest Configuration (`conftest.py`)
Create `<app_name>_test/conftest.py` to support maximized window rendering and prevent viewport clipping:

```python
import pytest

@pytest.fixture(scope="session")
def browser_context_args(browser_context_args):
    return {
        **browser_context_args,
        "no_viewport": True
    }

@pytest.fixture(scope="session")
def browser_type_launch_args(browser_type_launch_args):
    return {
        **browser_type_launch_args,
        "headless": False,             # Headed by default for interactive review
        "args": ["--start-maximized"]   # Launch fully maximized
    }
```

---

### Step 3: Centralized URL Configuration (`data/urls.py`)
Create `<app_name>_test/data/urls.py` so that switching domains or portal route prefixes requires editing only **one file**:

```python
import os

class AppURLs:
    # 1. Environment Domains
    ENV_DOMAINS = {
        "LOCAL": "http://localhost:3000",
        "QA": "https://qa.example.com",
        "UAT": "https://mutualfundbeta.abslmfbeta.com",
        "PROD": "https://mutualfund.adityabirlacapital.com",
    }
    ACTIVE_ENV = os.getenv("TEST_ENV", "UAT").upper()
    BASE_URL = ENV_DOMAINS.get(ACTIVE_ENV, ENV_DOMAINS["UAT"])

    # 2. Route Prefixes
    PORTAL_PREFIX = "/portal/investor"

    # 3. Route Paths (Relative)
    BROWSE_FUND_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/browsefund"
    FUND_SELECT_FLEXI_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/fund-select;fundcode=FOFSI"
    VALIDATE_PAN_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/validatePAN"
    FOLIO_DETAILS_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/folio-details"
    IDENTIFY_YOURSELF_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/identify-yourself"
    INVESTOR_DETAILS_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/investor-details"
    LUMPSUM_SIP_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/lumpsum-sip"
    CART_PATH = f"{PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/cart"

    # 4. Absolute URLs
    BROWSE_FUND_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{BROWSE_FUND_PATH}"
    VALIDATE_PAN_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{VALIDATE_PAN_PATH}"
    FOLIO_DETAILS_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{FOLIO_DETAILS_PATH}"
    IDENTIFY_YOURSELF_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{IDENTIFY_YOURSELF_PATH}"
    INVESTOR_DETAILS_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{INVESTOR_DETAILS_PATH}"
    LUMPSUM_SIP_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{LUMPSUM_SIP_PATH}"
    CART_URL = f"{BASE_URL}{CART_PATH}"

    @classmethod
    def get_fund_select_path(cls, fund_code: str = "FOFSI") -> str:
        return f"{cls.PORTAL_PREFIX}/quick-invest/fund-select;fundcode={fund_code}"
```

